Every opioid-first-taper-decision is a medication-taper-sequencing-decision.
Every benzodiazepine-first-taper-decision is a medication-taper-sequencing-decision.
Every careful-full-agonist-opioid-buprenorphine-transition-decision is a medication-taper-sequencing-decision.
If a patient receives an opioid at a current-opioid-dosage and receives a benzodiazepine at a current-benzodiazepine-dosage and a risk outweighs a benefit during a continued-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-therapy and there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician individualizes a medication-taper-sequencing-decision for the patient and reevaluates the medication-taper-sequencing-decision for the patient.
A buprenorphine-transition-example carefully occurs before a benzodiazepine-taper-example.
